  "scope": "The actual InfiniteDiagonalModel operator T on real lp exponent two, with natural coordinate j representing positive printed coordinate j+1.",
  "endpoints": {
    "T_not_closed_range": "¬ IsClosed (Set.range T)",
    "tendsto_T_hardPrefix": "Tendsto (fun N : ℕ => T (hardPrefix N)) atTop (𝓝 w)",
    "w_mem_closure_not_range": "w ∈ closure (Set.range T) ∧ w ∉ Set.range T"
  },
  "proof_routes": [
    "Unit coordinate has norm one and residual norm 1/(j+1); injectivity gives ker T = bottom; apply existing HilbertKernelProjection.not_closed_range_of_unit_witnesses.",
    "Use previously proved genuine hard-prefix residual square as reciprocal-square tail; continuity of square root gives norm convergence to w.",
    "An exact preimage of w would have every coordinate one, contradicting square summability."
  ],
